WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.083
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online C two, Book one.

2
00:00:05.383 --> 00:00:08.944
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.244 --> 00:00:16.935
Unit thirteen: Organizational Behavior. Today you will describe causal influences with influences / shapes / affects.

4
00:00:17.235 --> 00:00:19.748
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:23.724
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.583 --> 00:00:26.362
Organizational culture.

7
00:00:27.350 --> 00:00:33.088
Organizational culture means the shared values, beliefs and practices of an organisation.

8
00:00:33.683 --> 00:00:37.564
A blame-free organizational culture encourages honest reporting.

9
00:00:38.150 --> 00:00:41.650
Your turn. Say: Organizational culture.

10
00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:46.302
Organizational culture.

11
00:00:47.050 --> 00:00:48.225
Motivation.

12
00:00:49.217 --> 00:00:53.248
Motivation means the forces that drive people's effort and persistence.

13
00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:56.685
Intrinsic motivation outlasts any bonus.

14
00:00:57.283 --> 00:00:59.715
Your turn. Say: Motivation.

15
00:01:02.567 --> 00:01:03.661
Motivation.

16
00:01:04.417 --> 00:01:05.766
Group dynamics.

17
00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:10.131
Group dynamics means the patterns of interaction within a team.

18
00:01:10.717 --> 00:01:13.668
Group dynamics changed when the new manager arrived.

19
00:01:14.283 --> 00:01:17.388
Your turn. Say: Group dynamics.

20
00:01:20.233 --> 00:01:21.861
Group dynamics.

21
00:01:22.617 --> 00:01:23.629
Hierarchy.

22
00:01:24.617 --> 00:01:27.835
Hierarchy means a ranking of authority from top to bottom.

23
00:01:28.450 --> 00:01:31.982
A rigid hierarchy discouraged junior staff from speaking up.

24
00:01:32.583 --> 00:01:35.491
Your turn. Say: Hierarchy.

25
00:01:38.333 --> 00:01:39.439
Hierarchy.

26
00:01:40.183 --> 00:01:41.080
Norms.

27
00:01:42.083 --> 00:01:45.697
Norms means unwritten rules about acceptable behaviour.

28
00:01:46.283 --> 00:01:49.374
Team norms included replying to messages within a day.

29
00:01:49.983 --> 00:01:52.125
Your turn. Say: Norms.

30
00:01:54.967 --> 00:01:56.107
Norms.

31
00:01:56.850 --> 00:01:57.839
Cohesion.

32
00:01:58.850 --> 00:02:02.080
Cohesion means the degree to which group members are united.

33
00:02:02.683 --> 00:02:05.205
Shared challenges increased the team's cohesion.

34
00:02:05.817 --> 00:02:08.388
Your turn. Say: Cohesion.

35
00:02:11.233 --> 00:02:12.095
Cohesion.

36
00:02:12.850 --> 00:02:13.886
Conflict.

37
00:02:14.883 --> 00:02:17.788
Conflict means disagreement or tension between people.

38
00:02:18.383 --> 00:02:21.370
Managed well, conflict can generate better ideas.

39
00:02:21.983 --> 00:02:24.659
Your turn. Say: Conflict.

40
00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:28.559
Conflict.

41
00:02:29.317 --> 00:02:30.422
Productivity.

42
00:02:31.417 --> 00:02:35.413
Productivity means output relative to the effort or resources used.

43
00:02:36.017 --> 00:02:39.166
Recognition significantly influenced productivity.

44
00:02:39.750 --> 00:02:42.669
Your turn. Say: Productivity.

45
00:02:45.533 --> 00:02:46.569
Productivity.

46
00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:51.087
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:51.950 --> 00:02:58.050
Visal, two branches of the same bank have identical salaries and systems, but one performs far better. Why?

48
00:02:59.150 --> 00:03:09.755
Culture significantly shapes performance. In the stronger branch, the manager encourages questions, which affects how staff solve problems.

49
00:03:10.850 --> 00:03:13.836
Surely pay influences motivation more than culture?

50
00:03:14.950 --> 00:03:25.483
Pay affects whether people stay, but research suggests that recognition and autonomy influence daily effort far more strongly.

51
00:03:26.583 --> 00:03:28.943
Can a manager change a culture quickly?

52
00:03:30.050 --> 00:03:40.551
Not quickly, but consistently. Leaders' behaviour shapes norms, and norms gradually influence what everyone considers normal.

53
00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:43.409
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:44.250 --> 00:03:48.908
Grammar focus: Correlation language (influences, shapes, affects).

55
00:03:49.208 --> 00:03:50.453
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:51.150 --> 00:03:54.067
Culture significantly shapes employee motivation.

57
00:03:54.983 --> 00:03:57.854
Recognition strongly influences daily effort.

58
00:03:58.750 --> 00:04:01.760
Leaders' behaviour gradually affects team norms.

59
00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:10.168
These verbs take a direct object (affects motivation, not 'affects on'), but the nouns take 'on': an influence on, an effect on.

60
00:04:10.917 --> 00:04:14.475
Be careful! Don't say: Culture shapes on motivation.

61
00:04:16.433 --> 00:04:18.886
Say: Culture shapes motivation.

62
00:04:19.186 --> 00:04:21.359
Shape / affect take a direct object.

63
00:04:22.167 --> 00:04:24.656
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:25.467 --> 00:04:28.198
The Hawthorne Effect and Beyond.

65
00:04:28.498 --> 00:04:39.367
Organizational behaviour emerged partly from the Hawthorne studies of the 1920s, which found that workers' productivity was influenced by attention rather than lighting.

66
00:04:40.367 --> 00:04:47.800
Since then, researchers have shown that culture, norms and group dynamics shape performance as powerfully as formal structures.

67
00:04:48.800 --> 00:04:56.105
Self-determination theory argues that autonomy, competence and relatedness affect intrinsic motivation more strongly than external rewards.

68
00:04:57.100 --> 00:05:06.658
Hierarchy also matters: in steep hierarchies, junior employees may hesitate to report errors, with serious consequences in fields such as aviation and medicine.

69
00:05:07.667 --> 00:05:13.439
Understanding these influences enables leaders to design environments in which people choose to perform well.

70
00:05:14.533 --> 00:05:18.442
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:05:19.283 --> 00:05:21.353
Stress strongly blank concentration.

72
00:05:21.653 --> 00:05:25.550
A, affects on. B, affects. C, effects.

73
00:05:29.100 --> 00:05:31.216
The answer is B: affects.

74
00:05:32.350 --> 00:05:35.290
Unwritten rules about acceptable behaviour are blank.

75
00:05:35.590 --> 00:05:39.267
A, norms. B, hierarchy. C, cohesion.

76
00:05:42.800 --> 00:05:44.753
The answer is A: norms.

77
00:05:45.917 --> 00:05:48.729
The degree to which group members are united is blank.

78
00:05:49.029 --> 00:05:53.135
A, conflict. B, productivity. C, cohesion.

79
00:05:56.700 --> 00:05:58.897
The answer is C: cohesion.

80
00:06:00.050 --> 00:06:01.852
Choose the correct sentence.

81
00:06:02.152 --> 00:06:10.438
A, Culture has a strong effect on motivation.. B, Culture has a strong affect on motivation.. C, Culture effects strongly on motivation..

82
00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:17.811
The answer is A: Culture has a strong effect on motivation..

83
00:06:18.950 --> 00:06:23.875
According to the reading, the Hawthorne studies found productivity was influenced by…

84
00:06:24.175 --> 00:06:27.678
A, lighting. B, attention. C, salary.

85
00:06:31.233 --> 00:06:33.163
The answer is B: attention.

86
00:06:34.367 --> 00:06:37.704
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:06:38.550 --> 00:06:42.279
How does organizational culture influence employee motivation?

88
00:06:59.083 --> 00:07:00.502
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:07:00.802 --> 00:07:37.352
Organizational culture influences motivation by shaping what employees believe is valued, rewarded and safe. In a culture of trust, people take initiative because mistakes are treated as learning opportunities. By contrast, a culture of blame affects motivation negatively, since staff focus on protecting themselves rather than improving results. For example, a hospital where nurses can question doctors without fear tends to have fewer errors and more engaged staff. Culture, therefore, shapes effort every day.

90
00:07:37.652 --> 00:07:39.431
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:07:40.317 --> 00:07:46.510
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and correlation language (influences, shapes, affects).

92
00:07:46.810 --> 00:07:51.959
Today's value is collaboration. Work together, and share both the effort and the success.

93
00:07:52.259 --> 00:07:54.830
See you in Unit fourteen. Goodbye!

94
00:07:55.130 --> 00:07:57.677
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

